    prompt: `Write a video script for [platform: YouTube / TikTok / Instagram Reels / Product Demo]:\n\nPlatform-specific formats:\n\nYouTube (5-15 min educational/entertainment):\n- Hook (first 5-7 seconds): provocative question, surprising fact, or bold statement\n- Intro (15-30 sec): what you'll learn, why it matters, credibility\n- Body: 3-5 key points with examples, B-roll notes, screen recording cues\n- Pattern: Point → Example → Visual → Transition (repeat)\n- Summary: top 3 takeaways\n- CTA: subscribe, comment (ask specific question), watch next (end screen)\n- Outro: 5-10 seconds with channel branding\n\nTikTok / Reels (15-60 seconds, vertical):\n- Hook (first 1-2 seconds): text overlay + visual that grabs attention\n- Pattern: fast cuts, text-on-screen, trending audio\n- Single focused tip or observation (not multiple points)\n- Caption: expand on the video content, add keywords for discovery\n- CTA: follow, save, share, or comment\n\nProduct Demo (2-5 min, horizontal):\n- Problem statement (30 sec): show the pain point\n- Solution intro (30 sec): "That's why we built [product]"\n- Demo (60-120 sec): screen recording with voiceover, key features only\n- Social proof (30 sec): customer quote, metric, testimonial clip\n- Pricing + CTA (15 sec): where to sign up, special offer\n\nVisual cues to include in script:\n- [B-ROLL]: overlay footage while speaker continues\n- [SCREEN]: switch to screen recording\n- [TEXT OVERLAY]: key words to display on screen\n- [ZOOM]: camera zoom in for emphasis\n- [TRANSITION]: cut or transition type\n\nAudio notes:\n- Background music: energy level, genre reference\n- Sound effects: key moments that need emphasis\n- Voiceover vs. on-camera: indicate for each section\n\nTechnical production notes:\n- Aspect ratio: 16:9 (YouTube), 9:16 (TikTok/Reels)\n- Resolution: 1080p minimum, 4K for YouTube\n- Lighting setup: 3-point lighting description\n- Recording environment: minimize echo, background noise\n\nProvide the full script with timing estimates per section.`,
