    description: "Structure and write a comprehensive whitepaper or ebook that establishes thought leadership.",
    prompt: `Write a whitepaper/ebook on "[Topic]" to establish thought leadership:\n\nFront Matter:\n- Title: Compelling and specific (not generic)\n- Subtitle: What the reader will gain\n- Author name(s), company, publication date\n- Executive summary (1 page): key findings, who should read this, what they'll learn\n- Table of contents\n\nStructure (8-12 pages, ~3000-5000 words):\n\n1. Introduction (1 page):\n- The current state of the industry/topic\n- Why this topic matters right now (timeliness hook)\n- Key question this paper answers\n\n2. The Problem (2-3 pages):\n- Deep dive into the challenge or opportunity\n- Data/statistics that quantify the scope (with citations)\n- Common misconceptions or outdated approaches\n- Real-world examples of the problem in action\n\n3. The Framework / Methodology (3-4 pages):\n- Your unique approach, framework, or methodology\n- Step-by-step breakdown with diagrams\n- Case study or example applying the framework\n- Key principles or rules of thumb\n\n4. Implementation Guide (2-3 pages):\n- Practical steps to implement the framework\n- Tools and resources needed\n- Common pitfalls and how to avoid them\n- Timeline and resource estimates\n\n5. Future Outlook (1 page):\n- Where is this topic heading in the next 2-5 years?\n- What should readers prepare for?\n- Emerging trends to watch\n\n6. Conclusion (0.5 page):\n- Recap key takeaways\n- Call to action: next steps for the reader\n\nDesign specifications:\n- Professional layout with consistent typography hierarchy\n- Data visualizations: at least 3 charts/graphs (with source data)\n- Pull quotes from key insights\n- Callout boxes for definitions, tips, or important notes\n- Footnotes and references section\n- Author bio at the end (50 words each)\n\nLead generation elements:\n- Gated vs. ungated strategy recommendation\n- Landing page copy for the download page\n- Thank-you page with next-step CTA\n- Email nurture sequence (3 emails) for downloaders\n\nProvide the complete outline with key points for each section, data visualization descriptions, and the landing page copy.`,
