    prompt: `Create a VS Code extension skeleton for [extension purpose]:\n\nExtension Manifest (package.json):\n- activationEvents: when to activate (onCommand, onLanguage, onView, workspaceContains)\n- contributes.commands: command palette entries with title and category\n- contributes.views: custom views in sidebar/panel\n- contributes.viewsContainers: custom activity bar icon\n- contributes.configuration: extension settings with types and defaults\n- contributes.keybindings: keyboard shortcuts (when clause for context)\n- contributes.menus: right-click context menus, editor title bar buttons\n\nExtension Architecture (extension.ts):\n- activate(context: vscode.ExtensionContext):\n  - Register all commands, views, providers\n  - Setup status bar items\n  - Initialize output channel for logging\n- deactivate(): cleanup resources, subscriptions\n\nCommand Implementation:\n- Each command in its own file or function\n- Error handling: try/catch with vscode.window.showErrorMessage\n- Progress reporting: vscode.window.withProgress for long operations\n- User input: vscode.window.showInputBox, showQuickPick, showOpenDialog\n\nCustom Views (TreeView):\n- TreeDataProvider implementation:\n  - getChildren, getTreeItem, getParent\n  - Refresh when underlying data changes\n- TreeItem: label, iconPath, tooltip, contextValue, command, collapsibleState\n- Actions: inline buttons (edit, delete), context menu actions\n\nWebview Panels:\n- Create webview panel with HTML/CSS/JS\n- Message passing: postMessage and onDidReceiveMessage\n- Content Security Policy for webview security\n- Retain context when hidden (retainContextWhenHidden)\n- Theme-aware: use VS Code CSS variables for styling\n\nEditor Features:\n- Decorations: highlight text ranges, add gutters icons\n- Diagnostics: create diagnostic collection, push errors/warnings\n- CodeLens: actionable links above code\n- HoverProvider: show info on hover\n- CompletionItemProvider: auto-complete suggestions\n- DefinitionProvider: go-to-definition\n\nOutput & Logging:\n- OutputChannel for extension logs\n- Log level configuration (debug, info, warn, error)\n- Telemetry (opt-in): track feature usage, errors\n\nTesting:\n- Unit tests with @vscode/test-electron\n- Integration tests: launch VS Code, run commands, verify state\n- Test workspace with fixture files\n\nPublishing:\n- vsce package configuration\n- README with features, demo GIF, configuration options\n- CHANGELOG following Keep a Changelog\n- Publisher setup and PAT authentication\n\nProvide complete extension skeleton code and configuration.`,
