    icon: "&#x1F4E6;",
    title: "Monorepo Build System",
    description: "Set up a high-performance monorepo with shared configs, incremental builds, and dependency management.",
    prompt: `Set up a monorepo build system using [Turborepo / Nx / Lerna + pnpm workspaces]:\n\nRepository Structure:\n\`\`\`\n/apps/\n  web/          # Next.js / Vite frontend\n  api/          # Express / Fastify backend\n  mobile/       # React Native / Expo\n  docs/         # Documentation site\n/packages/\n  ui/           # Shared component library\n  utils/        # Shared utility functions\n  config/       # Shared configs (ESLint, TS, Jest, Prettier)\n  types/        # Shared TypeScript types\n  api-client/   # Generated API client\n/tooling/\n  eslint-config/\n  tsconfig/\n  jest-config/\n\`\`\`\n\nPackage Manager (pnpm):\n- pnpm-workspace.yaml defining workspace packages\n- Shared dependencies hoisted to root\n- Strict package boundaries (packages can only import their declared dependencies)\n- Overrides for forcing consistent versions across workspace\n\nBuild Orchestrator (Turborepo):\n- turbo.json pipeline configuration:\n  - build: dependsOn [^build], outputs [dist/, .next/]\n  - test: dependsOn [build], outputs []\n  - lint: no dependencies, can run in parallel\n  - typecheck: dependsOn [^build]\n- Caching: remote caching with Vercel or custom cache server\n- Incremental builds: only rebuild what changed\n- Parallel execution with dependency ordering\n\nShared Configuration:\n- TypeScript: base tsconfig.json with strict mode, path aliases\n- ESLint: shared rules with per-package overrides\n- Prettier: single config at root\n- Jest/Vitest: shared config with per-package setup\n- Environment variables: .env files per app, validation with zod\n\nDependency Management:\n- Renovate or Dependabot for automated updates\n- Check for duplicate dependencies across packages\n- Depcheck to find unused dependencies\n- Bundle analysis (size-limit) per package\n\nCI/CD:\n- Only build/test affected packages (--filter=[...since=origin/main])\n- Separate deploy pipelines per app\n- Release workflow: conventional commits → changesets → version bumps → changelog → npm publish\n\nDevelopment Experience:\n- Single dev command starts all apps (turbo dev)\n- Hot reload across packages (workspace references)\n- Shared dev database with Docker Compose\n- Storybook for UI component development\n\nProvide full configuration files, workspace setup script, and CI workflow.`,
