    prompt: `Build a TypeScript utility type library with these categories:\n\n1. Object Manipulation:\n- DeepPartial<T> — Make all properties optional recursively\n- DeepRequired<T> — Make all properties required recursively\n- DeepReadonly<T> — Make all properties readonly recursively\n- PickByType<T, U> — Pick properties whose values extend U\n- OmitByType<T, U> — Omit properties whose values extend U\n- Mutable<T> — Remove readonly from all properties\n- NonNullableProps<T> — Make all properties non-nullable\n\n2. Union and String:\n- Split<S, D> — Split string S by delimiter D into tuple\n- Join<T, D> — Join tuple of strings with delimiter\n- CamelCase<S> — Convert string to camelCase\n- KebabCase<S> — Convert string to kebab-case\n- StringToNumber<S> — Convert numeric string literal to number\n\n3. Function Types:\n- Parameters<T> — Extract parameters of function type (built-in but with examples)\n- ReturnType<T> — Extract return type (built-in but with examples)\n- AsyncReturnType<T> — Unwrap Promise from async function return type\n- CurriedFunction<T> — Auto-curry a function type\n- OverloadedParameters<T> — Extract parameters from all overloads\n\n4. Conditional and Mapped:\n- If<C, T, F> — Conditional type helper\n- IsNever<T> — Check if type is never\n- IsAny<T> — Check if type is any\n- IsUnion<T> — Check if type is a union\n- UnionToIntersection<U> — Convert union to intersection\n- LastOf<T> — Extract last element of a union\n\n5. Array and Tuple:\n- NonEmptyArray<T> — Array with at least one element\n- Head<T> — First element of tuple\n- Tail<T> — All elements except first\n- Unshift<T, U> — Prepend element to tuple\n- Reverse<T> — Reverse a tuple type\n- Flatten<T> — Flatten nested arrays\n- Filter<T, U> — Filter tuple elements by type\n\n6. Pattern-Specific:\n- DeepNonNullable<T> — Remove null/undefined recursively\n- Paths<T> — Get all dot-notation paths of an object\n- PathValue<T, P> — Get the type at a specific path\n- Merge<A, B> — Deep merge two types\n- Override<A, B> — Override properties of A with B\n\nFor each type provide:\n- The type definition\n- A plain-English explanation of what it does\n- At least 2 usage examples with expected results\n- Edge cases and limitations\n\nExport from index.ts with JSDoc documentation. Include a test file that type-checks all utilities.`,
